 "titulo": "Harvest tax in a Japanese village, 1700 🍶 Part 3 #history #shorts",
 "capa": "FOUR FOR THE LORD",
 "descripcion": "At harvest, the lord's officials measured the rice. A common rule: four parts for the lord, six for the people.\n\nSources: Edo-period nengu (annual rice tax), 'shikō rokumin'.\n\nCould you live on six?\n\n#history #edojapan #japanesehistory #historyfacts #shorts",
 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "October. The rice turns gold, and the whole village cuts it.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "You cut with a small sickle, one handful at a time.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "It dries on wooden racks, in long rows.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "Then you beat the stalks, to knock the grains loose.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "Then the lord's officials arrive, to measure the harvest.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "They walk the fields, and cut a sample square.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "From that one square, they decide the tax of the whole field.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "A common rule: four parts for the lord, six for the people.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "In a bad year, they may still ask for the same.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "Villages that couldn't pay sometimes rose up together.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "The village pays together, in straw bags of rice.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "The headman signs, and the bags go to the lord's storehouse.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "When the tax is paid, you finally celebrate.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "Everyone goes to the shrine, to thank the gods for the harvest.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "Drums, a shrine festival, and a cup of sake.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "For one night, nobody talks about tax.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "Four for the lord, six for you. Could you live on six?",
   "pausa": 0.3
  }
 ],
